The TypeScript adaptation implements only the triangular LFO and refuses the
sinusoidal default (it needs libm sin()), accepts only constant numeric option
values and named shape/interp constants, refuses timeline enable, LFO tables
whose uint32 index arithmetic could wrap and channel phases beyond int range,
refuses LFO lengths below one sample before output, always writes a new owned
output frame, declares the rings, delay_last and LFO table in reserve(),
enforces explicit allocation limits and AbortSignal, and adds no FFmpeg runtime
code. The original source and full notices remain in the pinned upstream
submodule.
